WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.370
Chaos and panic on the high sea – a constant challenge for the crew of the MV Aquarius.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.450
The vessel – staffed only with volunteers
- has run more than 100 rescue missions i

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.070
in the Mediterranean – and saved more than 15,000 migrants.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:23.730
Hauke Mack, Sea and Rescue Operator MV Aquarius:
“The current situation is disastrous.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:31.230
More and more people are coming, they're fleeing from Libya and it's very urgent that somebody

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:36.390
takes care of them as soon as possible, otherwise they will just drown and die.”

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:44.540
But the MV Aquarius and other N-G-O operated rescue vessels have recently come under fire.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:49.720
Several weeks ago, members of the right-wing group Generazione Identitaria blocked the

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.740
departure of the rescue ship.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.600
They claim that rescue boats are a pull-factor, attracting migrants and enticing smugglers.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.930
PTC Lars Scholtyssyk: “The proliferation
of charities operating rescue vessels in

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.950
the Mediterranean has be come one of the most controversial issue in this years'

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.310
migrant crisis here in Italy.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:11.670
The Italian government is therefore working on a code of conduct for NGOs that might severely

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.060
constrain their operations.”

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.740
Members of the European Parliament who visited the MV Aquarius last week, are criticizing

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.240
this move.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.060
 

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.159
“As if the NGOs were the problem – in this situation.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:30.950
With what we see in Syria, with what we see in Libya, with what we see in some African

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.310
countries where any fundamental right is constantly denied.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.770
I don't think NGOs are the problem.”

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:42.789
But the accusations have had an effect on
public opinion.

00:01:42.789 --> 00:01:50.240
Half of all Italians say the don't trust the
rescue charities.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.420
That's not fair, says parliamentarian Theresa
Reintke.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.920
Theresa Reintke, Member of the European Parliament:
“Actually this should not be their responsibility.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:05.130
These are civilians who have taken responsibility
for something that actually the European states

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:11.080
should have a responsibility for to organize
these search and rescue operations.”

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:17.300
So far this year, charities like the MV Aquarius
have carried out more than a third of all

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.810
rescues in the Mediterranean.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:25.250
While the recent surge in arrivals is once
again testing Italy's patience with the EU,

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.400
it seems the country is venting its frustration
on the aid workers.

